Let $h\in\mathbb Z[x]$ be prime-intersective, of degree at least two and with positive leading coefficient. There exist constants $c_h>0$ and $C_h\ge1$ such that, for every positive integer $N$ and every $A\subseteq[N]$, $$(A-A)\cap\{h(p):p\in\mathbb P\}\subseteq\{0\}
 \quad\Longrightarrow\quad
 |A|\le C_h N^{1-c_h}.$$

There is a constant $C_1$ such that for every sufficiently large $N$ and $1\le l\le N^\zeta$, $$\label{eq:descent-recurrence}
 \begin{split}
 \mathcal Y_l(N)\le {}&C_1N^{-\sigma}+(1+u_N)\biggl[
 (1-\rho_l)\mathcal Y_{lM_0}(n_\varnothing)\\
 &\hspace{12mm}+\rho_l
 \sum_{\substack{\varnothing\ne B\subseteq\mathcal P_N\\q_B\le N^\tau}}
       \eta_{l,B}\mathcal Y_{lD_B}(n_B)\biggr],\\
 u_N={}&(1+M_0^kN^{k\tau-1})^d-1=o(1).
 \end{split}$$ The constant and the sufficiently-large threshold are independent of $l$.

